			<div class="content" id="post-content-4066213">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Would they snap ur neck using anomalous means?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It could. It's a freakin' moving statue made of otherwise normal rebar and concrete. It operates based on principles completely unknown to science, who's to say it <em>can't</em> kill you using anomalous means?</p>
<p>Even if it uses it's &quot;arms&quot; to kill you, the thing moves <em>faster</em> than you can blink. You can't duck faster than you can blink; you'd have no way to avoid 173.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I am not going to say 173 is flawed but someone could have put more thought into this</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is probably the one time that I can say that you can't fault the original writer for the state of 173. 173 was the <em>first</em> SCP, and was <em>not</em> written with the intent to kickstart a collaborative writing site. It was, essentially, a random post placed on the /x/ board of 4chan.</p>

