														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2291285">
									

<p>Can you give me some directions? I keep trying to find the file or tale that has 173 vs. 682 but so far the closest I found was that mail-order-SCP magazine (am I the only one who loved the &quot;girls of SCP&quot; idea?) Also as a Doctor Who fangirl I can't help but notice that 173 operates EXACTLY like the Weeping Angels from the show with one or two exceptions. While both the weeping angels and 173 possess immense strength and mind blowing speed (&quot;They're fast, faster than you can believe.&quot; a quote from The Doctor in the episode &quot;Blink&quot;) Weeping Angels usually send their victim back in time with a touch so they can live off the potential energy of all that person's unfulfilled moments back in &quot;present day.&quot; To my knowledge there's only been one episode where the Weeping Angels went so far as to snap their victim's neck and that was to use the transmitter in his helmet to speak. Another difference is 173 can be monitored to some extent whereas even an image of a weeping angel can still kill you if you look away.</p>

